  "notes": "{下山|げざん} is the standard term for descending a mountain after climbing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {下山|げざん}する (descend a mountain)\n- {下山|げざん}ルート (descent route)\n- {下山|げざん}{開始|かいし} (begin the descent)\n- {安全|あんぜん}に{下山|げざん}する (descend safely)\n\nThe opposite is {登山|とざん} (climbing a mountain). Statistically, more accidents occur during {下山|げざん} than during {登山|とざん}, making it a frequently discussed topic in hiking safety.",
